window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b364-9bb151ec87b2f0fd.json"]={sha256:"9bb151ec87b2f0fde0cfe95b06d957c93ebd45389d376ef8e222613ed63c9b28",value:{"id":"b364","title":"鐵路回流與雜散電流控制","titleEn":"Rail-return and stray-current control","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"鐵路回流與雜散電流控制以「回路電位分流與雜散電荷控制」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。牽引回流、軌地電位與雜散電流是不同量；減少一處電位可能把電流轉向其他路徑，需用完整網路及時間電荷帳判斷。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops return potential current division and stray-charge control through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Traction return current, rail-earth potential and stray current are distinct; reducing voltage at one point can divert current elsewhere, requiring a complete network and time-integrated charge. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-power","subcategoryTitle":"牽引供電與受流","subcategoryTitleEn":"Traction power and current collection","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-power","learningTags":["rail","rail-power","power"],"architectureFamily":"rail-power","architectureNodes":[["列車回流","Train return"],["鋼軌接續","Rail bonds"],["軌地導納","Rail-earth conductance"],["收集路徑","Collection path"],["地電位參考","Earth-potential reference"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,0]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-power","labels":["列車回流","鋼軌接續","軌地導納","收集路徑","地電位參考"],"labelsEn":["Train return","Rail bonds","Rail-earth conductance","Collection path","Earth-potential reference"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm；y=I*R=15 V。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=16.5 V。模型邊界：穩態單一路徑；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm；y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A。只把 It 增加百分之十，y=366.667 A。模型邊界：兩個純電阻並聯；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm; y=I*R=15 V. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 V. Boundary: Steady single return path; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm; y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A. Increasing only It with a ten-percent increase gives y=366.667 A. Boundary: Two purely resistive parallel paths; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b364-v16-s1","title":"鋼軌回流壓降與平行回流分配","titleEn":"Rail-return voltage drop & Parallel return sharing","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼軌回流壓降」與「平行回流分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rail-return voltage drop\" and \"Parallel return sharing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b364-v16-01","title":"鋼軌回流壓降：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rail-return voltage drop: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「鋼軌回流壓降」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rail-return voltage drop” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"回流鋼軌有限電阻產生沿程電位差。本模型把 I 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16.5 V。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。穩態單一路徑。使用回流電流與兩點軌電位作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接續線劣化會增加局部壓降，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼軌回流壓降」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Finite return-rail resistance produces longitudinal potential difference. In this model, I is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 16.5 V. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Steady single return path. Use return current and rail potentials at two points as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A degraded bond increases local voltage drop; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rail-return voltage drop” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm；y=I*R=15 V。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm; y=I*R=15 V.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼軌回流壓降」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rail-return voltage drop”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-01-k1","title":"鋼軌回流壓降","titleEn":"Rail-return voltage drop","text":"回流鋼軌有限電阻產生沿程電位差。本模型把 I 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16.5 V。","textEn":"Finite return-rail resistance produces longitudinal potential difference. In this model, I is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼軌回流壓降」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rail-return voltage drop\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降","回流鋼軌有限電阻產生沿程電位差。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop.","Finite return-rail resistance produces longitudinal potential difference.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回流鋼軌有限電阻產生沿程電位差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Finite return-rail resistance produces longitudinal potential difference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b364-v16-02","title":"鋼軌回流壓降：定量估算","titleEn":"Rail-return voltage drop: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼軌回流壓降」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rail-return voltage drop” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm；y=I*R=15 V。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=16.5 V。模型邊界：穩態單一路徑；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm; y=I*R=15 V. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 V. Boundary: Steady single return path; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以回流電流與兩點軌電位區分模型與觀察，先用低壓電阻鏈與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use return current and rail potentials at two points to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm；y=I*R=15 V。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=16.5 V。模型邊界：穩態單一路徑；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm; y=I*R=15 V. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 V. Boundary: Steady single return path; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼軌回流壓降」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rail-return voltage drop\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm；y=I*R=15 V。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm; y=I*R=15 V."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm；y=I*R=15 V。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=1000 A, R=0.015 ohm; y=I*R=15 V. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b364-v16-03","title":"鋼軌回流壓降：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rail-return voltage drop: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼軌回流壓降」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rail-return voltage drop” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以回流電流與兩點軌電位區分模型與觀察，先用低壓電阻鏈與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「鋼軌回流壓降」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use return current and rail potentials at two points to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage resistor chain and differential voltmeter, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rail-return voltage drop. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「鋼軌回流壓降」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出穩態單一路徑如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接續線劣化會增加局部壓降造成偏離的合成觀察，以回流電流與兩點軌電位說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rail-return voltage drop, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Steady single return path. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. Explain which evidence in return current and rail potentials at two points distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以回流電流與兩點軌電位區分模型與觀察，先用低壓電阻鏈與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「鋼軌回流壓降」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use return current and rail potentials at two points to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage resistor chain and differential voltmeter, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rail-return voltage drop. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「鋼軌回流壓降」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出穩態單一路徑如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接續線劣化會增加局部壓降造成偏離的合成觀察，以回流電流與兩點軌電位說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rail-return voltage drop, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Steady single return path. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. Explain which evidence in return current and rail potentials at two points distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼軌回流壓降」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rail-return voltage drop\"?","options":["本單元以回流電流與兩點軌電位區分模型與觀察，先用低壓電阻鏈與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何"],"optionsEn":["Use return current and rail potentials at two points to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以回流電流與兩點軌電位區分模型與觀察，先用低壓電阻鏈與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use return current and rail potentials at two points to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b364-v16-04","title":"鋼軌回流壓降：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rail-return voltage drop: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼軌回流壓降」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rail-return voltage drop” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接續線劣化會增加局部壓降。這個失效與「鋼軌回流壓降」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查回流電流與兩點軌電位，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. This failure and a measurement bias in Rail-return voltage drop can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check return current and rail potentials at two points rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用回流電流與兩點軌電位作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接續線劣化會增加局部壓降，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接續線劣化會增加局部壓降。這個失效與「鋼軌回流壓降」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查回流電流與兩點軌電位，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. This failure and a measurement bias in Rail-return voltage drop can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check return current and rail potentials at two points rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼軌回流壓降」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rail-return voltage drop\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","接續線劣化會增加局部壓降。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A degraded bond increases local voltage drop.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接續線劣化會增加局部壓降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A degraded bond increases local voltage drop. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b364-v16-05","title":"平行回流分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel return sharing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「平行回流分配」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel return sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平行路徑以相同端電壓按電阻反比分流。本模型把 It 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 366.667 A。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。兩個純電阻並聯。使用鋼軌與回流線電流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；一路中斷會重分配全回路電流，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平行回流分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Parallel paths share terminal voltage and divide current inversely with resistance. In this model, It is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 366.667 A. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Two purely resistive parallel paths. Use rail and return-cable currents as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Opening one path redistributes total return current; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel return sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm；y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm; y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平行回流分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel return sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-05-k1","title":"平行回流分配","titleEn":"Parallel return sharing","text":"平行路徑以相同端電壓按電阻反比分流。本模型把 It 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 366.667 A。","textEn":"Parallel paths share terminal voltage and divide current inversely with resistance. In this model, It is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平行回流分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel return sharing\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段","平行路徑以相同端電壓按電阻反比分流。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.","Parallel paths share terminal voltage and divide current inversely with resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平行路徑以相同端電壓按電阻反比分流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Parallel paths share terminal voltage and divide current inversely with resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b364-v16-06","title":"平行回流分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel return sharing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平行回流分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel return sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm；y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A。只把 It 增加百分之十，y=366.667 A。模型邊界：兩個純電阻並聯；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm; y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A. Increasing only It with a ten-percent increase gives y=366.667 A. Boundary: Two purely resistive parallel paths; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以鋼軌與回流線電流區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓支路電流量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rail and return-cable currents to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm；y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A。只把 It 增加百分之十，y=366.667 A。模型邊界：兩個純電阻並聯；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm; y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A. Increasing only It with a ten-percent increase gives y=366.667 A. Boundary: Two purely resistive parallel paths; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平行回流分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel return sharing\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm; y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm；y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: It=1000 A, Rrail=0.02 ohm, Rcable=0.01 ohm; y=It*Rcable/(Rrail+Rcable)=333.333 A. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b364-v16-07","title":"平行回流分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel return sharing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平行回流分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel return sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以鋼軌與回流線電流區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓支路電流量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平行回流分配」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rail and return-cable currents to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using isolated low-voltage branch-current measurements, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Parallel return sharing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「平行回流分配」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩個純電阻並聯如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由一路中斷會重分配全回路電流造成偏離的合成觀察，以鋼軌與回流線電流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Parallel return sharing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Two purely resistive parallel paths. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current. Explain which evidence in rail and return-cable currents distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Opening one path redistributes total return current. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以鋼軌與回流線電流區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓支路電流量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平行回流分配」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use rail and return-cable currents to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using isolated low-voltage branch-current measurements, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Parallel return sharing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「平行回流分配」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩個純電阻並聯如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由一路中斷會重分配全回路電流造成偏離的合成觀察，以鋼軌與回流線電流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Parallel return sharing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Two purely resistive parallel paths. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current. Explain which evidence in rail and return-cable currents distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平行回流分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel return sharing\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以鋼軌與回流線電流區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓支路電流量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use rail and return-cable currents to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以鋼軌與回流線電流區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓支路電流量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rail and return-cable currents to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b364-v16-08","title":"平行回流分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel return sharing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平行回流分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel return sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一路中斷會重分配全回路電流。這個失效與「平行回流分配」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查鋼軌與回流線電流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Opening one path redistributes total return current. This failure and a measurement bias in Parallel return sharing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail and return-cable currents rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用鋼軌與回流線電流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；一路中斷會重分配全回路電流，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Opening one path redistributes total return current; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一路中斷會重分配全回路電流。這個失效與「平行回流分配」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查鋼軌與回流線電流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Opening one path redistributes total return current. This failure and a measurement bias in Parallel return sharing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail and return-cable currents rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平行回流分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel return sharing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段","一路中斷會重分配全回路電流。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.","Opening one path redistributes total return current."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一路中斷會重分配全回路電流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Opening one path redistributes total return current. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b364-v16-s2","title":"軌地漏流導納與漏流時間電荷","titleEn":"Rail-earth leakage conductance & Leakage charge accumulation","description":"本階段聚焦「軌地漏流導納」與「漏流時間電荷」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rail-earth leakage conductance\" and \"Leakage charge accumulation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b364-v16-09","title":"軌地漏流導納：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rail-earth leakage conductance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「軌地漏流導納」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rail-earth leakage conductance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分布導納乘長度與電位得到均勻漏流近似。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.44 A。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻電位與導納。使用軌地電位及分段導納作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軌地漏流導納」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distributed conductance times length and potential approximates uniform leakage. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.44 A. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform potential and conductance. Use rail-earth potential and segmented conductance as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rail-earth leakage conductance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km；y=V*G*L=0.4 A。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km; y=V*G*L=0.4 A.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軌地漏流導納」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rail-earth leakage conductance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-09-k1","title":"軌地漏流導納","titleEn":"Rail-earth leakage conductance","text":"分布導納乘長度與電位得到均勻漏流近似。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.44 A。","textEn":"Distributed conductance times length and potential approximates uniform leakage. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軌地漏流導納」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rail-earth leakage conductance\" is correct?","options":["分布導納乘長度與電位得到均勻漏流近似。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段"],"optionsEn":["Distributed conductance times length and potential approximates uniform leakage.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分布導納乘長度與電位得到均勻漏流近似。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distributed conductance times length and potential approximates uniform leakage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b364-v16-10","title":"軌地漏流導納：定量估算","titleEn":"Rail-earth leakage conductance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軌地漏流導納」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rail-earth leakage conductance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km；y=V*G*L=0.4 A。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=0.44 A。模型邊界：均勻電位與導納；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km; y=V*G*L=0.4 A. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.44 A. Boundary: Uniform potential and conductance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以軌地電位及分段導納區分模型與觀察，先用低壓梯形電阻網路建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use rail-earth potential and segmented conductance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km；y=V*G*L=0.4 A。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=0.44 A。模型邊界：均勻電位與導納；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km; y=V*G*L=0.4 A. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.44 A. Boundary: Uniform potential and conductance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軌地漏流導納」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rail-earth leakage conductance\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km；y=V*G*L=0.4 A。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km; y=V*G*L=0.4 A.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km；y=V*G*L=0.4 A。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=10 V, G=0.02 S/km, L=2 km; y=V*G*L=0.4 A. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b364-v16-11","title":"軌地漏流導納：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rail-earth leakage conductance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軌地漏流導納」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rail-earth leakage conductance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以軌地電位及分段導納區分模型與觀察，先用低壓梯形電阻網路建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌地漏流導納」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use rail-earth potential and segmented conductance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage ladder-resistor network, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rail-earth leakage conductance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「軌地漏流導納」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻電位與導納如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌地電位及分段導納說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rail-earth leakage conductance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform potential and conductance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. Explain which evidence in rail-earth potential and segmented conductance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以軌地電位及分段導納區分模型與觀察，先用低壓梯形電阻網路建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「軌地漏流導納」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use rail-earth potential and segmented conductance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage ladder-resistor network, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Rail-earth leakage conductance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「軌地漏流導納」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻電位與導納如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段造成偏離的合成觀察，以軌地電位及分段導納說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Rail-earth leakage conductance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform potential and conductance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. Explain which evidence in rail-earth potential and segmented conductance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軌地漏流導納」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rail-earth leakage conductance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流","本單元以軌地電位及分段導納區分模型與觀察，先用低壓梯形電阻網路建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals.","Use rail-earth potential and segmented conductance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以軌地電位及分段導納區分模型與觀察，先用低壓梯形電阻網路建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use rail-earth potential and segmented conductance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b364-v16-12","title":"軌地漏流導納：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rail-earth leakage conductance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軌地漏流導納」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rail-earth leakage conductance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段。這個失效與「軌地漏流導納」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌地電位及分段導納，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. This failure and a measurement bias in Rail-earth leakage conductance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail-earth potential and segmented conductance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用軌地電位及分段導納作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段。這個失效與「軌地漏流導納」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查軌地電位及分段導納，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. This failure and a measurement bias in Rail-earth leakage conductance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check rail-earth potential and segmented conductance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軌地漏流導納」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rail-earth leakage conductance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段"],"optionsEn":["Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods."],"answer":0,"explanation":"軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b364-v16-13","title":"漏流時間電荷：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Leakage charge accumulation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「漏流時間電荷」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Leakage charge accumulation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"腐蝕相關量需按電流方向與時間積分。本模型把 I 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6336 C。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定方向常電流。使用電流正負與持續時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漏流時間電荷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Corrosion-related accounting needs current direction integrated over time. In this model, I is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 6336 C. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Constant current with a fixed direction. Use current sign and duration as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Leakage charge accumulation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=0.2 A, hours=8 h；y=I*hours*3600=5760 C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=0.2 A, hours=8 h; y=I*hours*3600=5760 C.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漏流時間電荷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Leakage charge accumulation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-13-k1","title":"漏流時間電荷","titleEn":"Leakage charge accumulation","text":"腐蝕相關量需按電流方向與時間積分。本模型把 I 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6336 C。","textEn":"Corrosion-related accounting needs current direction integrated over time. In this model, I is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漏流時間電荷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Leakage charge accumulation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段","腐蝕相關量需按電流方向與時間積分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods.","Corrosion-related accounting needs current direction integrated over time.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"腐蝕相關量需按電流方向與時間積分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Corrosion-related accounting needs current direction integrated over time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b364-v16-14","title":"漏流時間電荷：定量估算","titleEn":"Leakage charge accumulation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漏流時間電荷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Leakage charge accumulation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=0.2 A, hours=8 h；y=I*hours*3600=5760 C。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=6336 C。模型邊界：固定方向常電流；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=0.2 A, hours=8 h; y=I*hours*3600=5760 C. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=6336 C. Boundary: Constant current with a fixed direction; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以電流正負與持續時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成有號電流時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use current sign and duration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=0.2 A, hours=8 h；y=I*hours*3600=5760 C。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=6336 C。模型邊界：固定方向常電流；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=0.2 A, hours=8 h; y=I*hours*3600=5760 C. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=6336 C. Boundary: Constant current with a fixed direction; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漏流時間電荷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Leakage charge accumulation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=0.2 A, hours=8 h；y=I*hours*3600=5760 C。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=0.2 A, hours=8 h; y=I*hours*3600=5760 C."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=0.2 A, hours=8 h；y=I*hours*3600=5760 C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=0.2 A, hours=8 h; y=I*hours*3600=5760 C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b364-v16-15","title":"漏流時間電荷：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Leakage charge accumulation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漏流時間電荷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Leakage charge accumulation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以電流正負與持續時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成有號電流時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「漏流時間電荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use current sign and duration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic signed current time series, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Leakage charge accumulation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「漏流時間電荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定方向常電流如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段造成偏離的合成觀察，以電流正負與持續時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Leakage charge accumulation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant current with a fixed direction. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. Explain which evidence in current sign and duration distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以電流正負與持續時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成有號電流時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「漏流時間電荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use current sign and duration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic signed current time series, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Leakage charge accumulation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「漏流時間電荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定方向常電流如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段造成偏離的合成觀察，以電流正負與持續時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Leakage charge accumulation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant current with a fixed direction. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. Explain which evidence in current sign and duration distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漏流時間電荷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Leakage charge accumulation\"?","options":["本單元以電流正負與持續時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成有號電流時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降"],"optionsEn":["Use current sign and duration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以電流正負與持續時間區分模型與觀察，先用合成有號電流時間序列建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use current sign and duration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b364-v16-16","title":"漏流時間電荷：失效診斷","titleEn":"Leakage charge accumulation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漏流時間電荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Leakage charge accumulation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段。這個失效與「漏流時間電荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查電流正負與持續時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. This failure and a measurement bias in Leakage charge accumulation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check current sign and duration rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用電流正負與持續時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段。這個失效與「漏流時間電荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查電流正負與持續時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. This failure and a measurement bias in Leakage charge accumulation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check current sign and duration rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏流時間電荷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Leakage charge accumulation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b364-v16-s3","title":"理想法拉第質量與接續電阻增加","titleEn":"Ideal Faraday mass & Bond-resistance increase","description":"本階段聚焦「理想法拉第質量」與「接續電阻增加」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ideal Faraday mass\" and \"Bond-resistance increase\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b364-v16-17","title":"理想法拉第質量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ideal Faraday mass: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「理想法拉第質量」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ideal Faraday mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"電荷依價數與莫耳質量換算理想溶解量。本模型把 Q 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.83362 g。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。假定鐵二價且百分百電流效率。使用陽極電荷與材料狀態作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「理想法拉第質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Charge converts to ideal dissolution mass through valence and molar mass. In this model, Q is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1.83362 g. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Assumed divalent iron at one hundred percent current efficiency. Use anodic charge and material condition as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ideal Faraday mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol；y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol; y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「理想法拉第質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ideal Faraday mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-17-k1","title":"理想法拉第質量","titleEn":"Ideal Faraday mass","text":"電荷依價數與莫耳質量換算理想溶解量。本模型把 Q 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.83362 g。","textEn":"Charge converts to ideal dissolution mass through valence and molar mass. In this model, Q is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「理想法拉第質量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ideal Faraday mass\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢","電荷依價數與莫耳質量換算理想溶解量。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","Charge converts to ideal dissolution mass through valence and molar mass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電荷依價數與莫耳質量換算理想溶解量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Charge converts to ideal dissolution mass through valence and molar mass. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b364-v16-18","title":"理想法拉第質量：定量估算","titleEn":"Ideal Faraday mass: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「理想法拉第質量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ideal Faraday mass” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol；y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g。只把 Q 增加百分之十，y=1.83362 g。模型邊界：假定鐵二價且百分百電流效率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol; y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g. Increasing only Q with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.83362 g. Boundary: Assumed divalent iron at one hundred percent current efficiency; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以陽極電荷與材料狀態區分模型與觀察，先用紙上電荷帳與材料假設建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use anodic charge and material condition to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol；y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g。只把 Q 增加百分之十，y=1.83362 g。模型邊界：假定鐵二價且百分百電流效率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol; y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g. Increasing only Q with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.83362 g. Boundary: Assumed divalent iron at one hundred percent current efficiency; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「理想法拉第質量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ideal Faraday mass\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol; y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol；y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=5760 C, M=55.845 g/mol, z=2 1, F=96485 C/mol; y=Q*M/(z*F)=1.66693 g. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b364-v16-19","title":"理想法拉第質量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ideal Faraday mass: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「理想法拉第質量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ideal Faraday mass” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以陽極電荷與材料狀態區分模型與觀察，先用紙上電荷帳與材料假設建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「理想法拉第質量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use anodic charge and material condition to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paper charge ledger and material assumptions, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ideal Faraday mass. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「理想法拉第質量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出假定鐵二價且百分百電流效率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同造成偏離的合成觀察，以陽極電荷與材料狀態說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ideal Faraday mass, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Assumed divalent iron at one hundred percent current efficiency. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. Explain which evidence in anodic charge and material condition distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以陽極電荷與材料狀態區分模型與觀察，先用紙上電荷帳與材料假設建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「理想法拉第質量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use anodic charge and material condition to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paper charge ledger and material assumptions, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Ideal Faraday mass. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「理想法拉第質量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出假定鐵二價且百分百電流效率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同造成偏離的合成觀察，以陽極電荷與材料狀態說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Ideal Faraday mass, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Assumed divalent iron at one hundred percent current efficiency. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. Explain which evidence in anodic charge and material condition distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「理想法拉第質量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ideal Faraday mass\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以陽極電荷與材料狀態區分模型與觀察，先用紙上電荷帳與材料假設建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use anodic charge and material condition to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以陽極電荷與材料狀態區分模型與觀察，先用紙上電荷帳與材料假設建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use anodic charge and material condition to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b364-v16-20","title":"理想法拉第質量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ideal Faraday mass: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「理想法拉第質量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ideal Faraday mass” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同。這個失效與「理想法拉第質量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查陽極電荷與材料狀態，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. This failure and a measurement bias in Ideal Faraday mass can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check anodic charge and material condition rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用陽極電荷與材料狀態作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同。這個失效與「理想法拉第質量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查陽極電荷與材料狀態，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. This failure and a measurement bias in Ideal Faraday mass can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check anodic charge and material condition rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「理想法拉第質量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ideal Faraday mass\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢","電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b364-v16-21","title":"接續電阻增加：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bond-resistance increase: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「接續電阻增加」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bond-resistance increase” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相對增幅應與絕對電阻及量測解析度一起讀。本模型把 Rnew 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 340 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。相同溫度的電阻比較。使用接續四線電阻與溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接續電阻增加」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Relative increase needs absolute resistance and measurement resolution. In this model, Rnew is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 340 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Resistance comparison at matched temperature. Use four-terminal bond resistance and temperature as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bond-resistance increase” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm；y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm; y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接續電阻增加」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bond-resistance increase”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-21-k1","title":"接續電阻增加","titleEn":"Bond-resistance increase","text":"相對增幅應與絕對電阻及量測解析度一起讀。本模型把 Rnew 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 340 percent。","textEn":"Relative increase needs absolute resistance and measurement resolution. In this model, Rnew is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接續電阻增加」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bond-resistance increase\" is correct?","options":["相對增幅應與絕對電阻及量測解析度一起讀。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果"],"optionsEn":["Relative increase needs absolute resistance and measurement resolution.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相對增幅應與絕對電阻及量測解析度一起讀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Relative increase needs absolute resistance and measurement resolution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b364-v16-22","title":"接續電阻增加：定量估算","titleEn":"Bond-resistance increase: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接續電阻增加」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bond-resistance increase” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm；y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent。只把 Rnew 增加百分之十，y=340 percent。模型邊界：相同溫度的電阻比較；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm; y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent. Increasing only Rnew with a ten-percent increase gives y=340 percent. Boundary: Resistance comparison at matched temperature; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以接續四線電阻與溫度區分模型與觀察，先用低壓四線比較量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use four-terminal bond resistance and temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm；y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent。只把 Rnew 增加百分之十，y=340 percent。模型邊界：相同溫度的電阻比較；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm; y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent. Increasing only Rnew with a ten-percent increase gives y=340 percent. Boundary: Resistance comparison at matched temperature; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接續電阻增加」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bond-resistance increase\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm; y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm；y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: Rnew=0.8 mohm, Rbase=0.2 mohm; y=(Rnew-Rbase)/Rbase*100=300 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b364-v16-23","title":"接續電阻增加：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bond-resistance increase: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接續電阻增加」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bond-resistance increase” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以接續四線電阻與溫度區分模型與觀察，先用低壓四線比較量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接續電阻增加」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use four-terminal bond resistance and temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage four-terminal comparison, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bond-resistance increase. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「接續電阻增加」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出相同溫度的電阻比較如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢造成偏離的合成觀察，以接續四線電阻與溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bond-resistance increase, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Resistance comparison at matched temperature. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. Explain which evidence in four-terminal bond resistance and temperature distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以接續四線電阻與溫度區分模型與觀察，先用低壓四線比較量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接續電阻增加」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use four-terminal bond resistance and temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage four-terminal comparison, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bond-resistance increase. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「接續電阻增加」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出相同溫度的電阻比較如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢造成偏離的合成觀察，以接續四線電阻與溫度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bond-resistance increase, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Resistance comparison at matched temperature. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. Explain which evidence in four-terminal bond resistance and temperature distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接續電阻增加」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bond-resistance increase\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段","本單元以接續四線電阻與溫度區分模型與觀察，先用低壓四線比較量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.","Use four-terminal bond resistance and temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以接續四線電阻與溫度區分模型與觀察，先用低壓四線比較量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use four-terminal bond resistance and temperature to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b364-v16-24","title":"接續電阻增加：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bond-resistance increase: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接續電阻增加」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bond-resistance increase” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢。這個失效與「接續電阻增加」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接續四線電阻與溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. This failure and a measurement bias in Bond-resistance increase can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check four-terminal bond resistance and temperature rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用接續四線電阻與溫度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢。這個失效與「接續電阻增加」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接續四線電阻與溫度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. This failure and a measurement bias in Bond-resistance increase can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check four-terminal bond resistance and temperature rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接續電阻增加」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bond-resistance increase\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果"],"optionsEn":["Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b364-v16-s4","title":"收集回路比例與土壤均勻電阻","titleEn":"Collection-circuit current fraction & Uniform soil-path resistance","description":"本階段聚焦「收集回路比例」與「土壤均勻電阻」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Collection-circuit current fraction\" and \"Uniform soil-path resistance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b364-v16-25","title":"收集回路比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Collection-circuit current fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「收集回路比例」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Collection-circuit current fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"收集比例只描述定義邊界內的電流帳。本模型把 collected 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 79.2 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。同時窗閉合電流帳。使用收集與未收集分流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「收集回路比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Collection fraction describes current accounting within a defined boundary. In this model, collected is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 79.2 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Closed current balance over one time window. Use collected and uncollected branches as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Collection-circuit current fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A；y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A; y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「收集回路比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Collection-circuit current fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-25-k1","title":"收集回路比例","titleEn":"Collection-circuit current fraction","text":"收集比例只描述定義邊界內的電流帳。本模型把 collected 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 79.2 percent。","textEn":"Collection fraction describes current accounting within a defined boundary. In this model, collected is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「收集回路比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Collection-circuit current fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果","收集比例只描述定義邊界內的電流帳。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness.","Collection fraction describes current accounting within a defined boundary.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"收集比例只描述定義邊界內的電流帳。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Collection fraction describes current accounting within a defined boundary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b364-v16-26","title":"收集回路比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Collection-circuit current fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「收集回路比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Collection-circuit current fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A；y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent。只把 collected 增加百分之十，y=79.2 percent。模型邊界：同時窗閉合電流帳；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A; y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent. Increasing only collected with a ten-percent increase gives y=79.2 percent. Boundary: Closed current balance over one time window; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以收集與未收集分流區分模型與觀察，先用分支低壓電流表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use collected and uncollected branches to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A；y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent。只把 collected 增加百分之十，y=79.2 percent。模型邊界：同時窗閉合電流帳；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A; y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent. Increasing only collected with a ten-percent increase gives y=79.2 percent. Boundary: Closed current balance over one time window; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「收集回路比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Collection-circuit current fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A; y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A；y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: collected=0.18 A, leakage=0.25 A; y=collected/leakage*100=72 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b364-v16-27","title":"收集回路比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Collection-circuit current fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「收集回路比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Collection-circuit current fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以收集與未收集分流區分模型與觀察，先用分支低壓電流表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「收集回路比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use collected and uncollected branches to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using branch low-voltage ammeters, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Collection-circuit current fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「收集回路比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同時窗閉合電流帳如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果造成偏離的合成觀察，以收集與未收集分流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Collection-circuit current fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Closed current balance over one time window. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. Explain which evidence in collected and uncollected branches distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以收集與未收集分流區分模型與觀察，先用分支低壓電流表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「收集回路比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use collected and uncollected branches to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using branch low-voltage ammeters, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Collection-circuit current fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「收集回路比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出同時窗閉合電流帳如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果造成偏離的合成觀察，以收集與未收集分流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Collection-circuit current fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Closed current balance over one time window. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. Explain which evidence in collected and uncollected branches distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「收集回路比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Collection-circuit current fraction\"?","options":["本單元以收集與未收集分流區分模型與觀察，先用分支低壓電流表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段"],"optionsEn":["Use collected and uncollected branches to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以收集與未收集分流區分模型與觀察，先用分支低壓電流表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use collected and uncollected branches to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b364-v16-28","title":"收集回路比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Collection-circuit current fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「收集回路比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Collection-circuit current fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果。這個失效與「收集回路比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查收集與未收集分流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. This failure and a measurement bias in Collection-circuit current fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check collected and uncollected branches rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用收集與未收集分流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果。這個失效與「收集回路比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查收集與未收集分流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. This failure and a measurement bias in Collection-circuit current fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check collected and uncollected branches rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「收集回路比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Collection-circuit current fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b364-v16-29","title":"土壤均勻電阻：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Uniform soil-path resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「土壤均勻電阻」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Uniform soil-path resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土壤電阻率需幾何路徑才能換成電阻。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 22 ohm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。僅均勻等截面教學路徑。使用土壤含水及電極幾何作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「土壤均勻電阻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Soil resistivity needs path geometry before becoming resistance. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 22 ohm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform constant-area teaching path only. Use soil moisture and electrode geometry as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Uniform soil-path resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2；y=rho*L/A=20 ohm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2; y=rho*L/A=20 ohm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「土壤均勻電阻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Uniform soil-path resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-29-k1","title":"土壤均勻電阻","titleEn":"Uniform soil-path resistance","text":"土壤電阻率需幾何路徑才能換成電阻。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 22 ohm。","textEn":"Soil resistivity needs path geometry before becoming resistance. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「土壤均勻電阻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Uniform soil-path resistance\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差","土壤電阻率需幾何路徑才能換成電阻。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.","Soil resistivity needs path geometry before becoming resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"土壤電阻率需幾何路徑才能換成電阻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Soil resistivity needs path geometry before becoming resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b364-v16-30","title":"土壤均勻電阻：定量估算","titleEn":"Uniform soil-path resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「土壤均勻電阻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Uniform soil-path resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2；y=rho*L/A=20 ohm。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=22 ohm。模型邊界：僅均勻等截面教學路徑；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2; y=rho*L/A=20 ohm. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=22 ohm. Boundary: Uniform constant-area teaching path only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以土壤含水及電極幾何區分模型與觀察，先用電阻率資料與紙上幾何建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use soil moisture and electrode geometry to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2；y=rho*L/A=20 ohm。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=22 ohm。模型邊界：僅均勻等截面教學路徑；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2; y=rho*L/A=20 ohm. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=22 ohm. Boundary: Uniform constant-area teaching path only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「土壤均勻電阻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Uniform soil-path resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2；y=rho*L/A=20 ohm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2; y=rho*L/A=20 ohm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2；y=rho*L/A=20 ohm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=100 ohm*m, L=2 m, A=10 m2; y=rho*L/A=20 ohm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b364-v16-31","title":"土壤均勻電阻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Uniform soil-path resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「土壤均勻電阻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Uniform soil-path resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以土壤含水及電極幾何區分模型與觀察，先用電阻率資料與紙上幾何建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「土壤均勻電阻」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use soil moisture and electrode geometry to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using resistivity data and paper geometry, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Uniform soil-path resistance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「土壤均勻電阻」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出僅均勻等截面教學路徑如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何造成偏離的合成觀察，以土壤含水及電極幾何說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Uniform soil-path resistance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform constant-area teaching path only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. Explain which evidence in soil moisture and electrode geometry distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以土壤含水及電極幾何區分模型與觀察，先用電阻率資料與紙上幾何建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「土壤均勻電阻」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use soil moisture and electrode geometry to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using resistivity data and paper geometry, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Uniform soil-path resistance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「土壤均勻電阻」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出僅均勻等截面教學路徑如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何造成偏離的合成觀察，以土壤含水及電極幾何說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Uniform soil-path resistance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform constant-area teaching path only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. Explain which evidence in soil moisture and electrode geometry distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「土壤均勻電阻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Uniform soil-path resistance\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以土壤含水及電極幾何區分模型與觀察，先用電阻率資料與紙上幾何建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use soil moisture and electrode geometry to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以土壤含水及電極幾何區分模型與觀察，先用電阻率資料與紙上幾何建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use soil moisture and electrode geometry to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b364-v16-32","title":"土壤均勻電阻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Uniform soil-path resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「土壤均勻電阻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Uniform soil-path resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何。這個失效與「土壤均勻電阻」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查土壤含水及電極幾何，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. This failure and a measurement bias in Uniform soil-path resistance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check soil moisture and electrode geometry rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用土壤含水及電極幾何作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何。這個失效與「土壤均勻電阻」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查土壤含水及電極幾何，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. This failure and a measurement bias in Uniform soil-path resistance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check soil moisture and electrode geometry rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「土壤均勻電阻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Uniform soil-path resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差","真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.","Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"真實擴散電流不能套等截面直棒幾何。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Real spreading current does not follow constant-area bar geometry. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b364-v16-s5","title":"參考電極偏移與時間取樣電荷","titleEn":"Reference-electrode offset & Sampled charge estimate","description":"本階段聚焦「參考電極偏移」與「時間取樣電荷」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Reference-electrode offset\" and \"Sampled charge estimate\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b364-v16-33","title":"參考電極偏移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reference-electrode offset: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「參考電極偏移」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reference-electrode offset” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"參考電極自身偏差會平移所有量測電位。本模型把 measured 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.73 V。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。已知固定加性偏差。使用獨立參考與校正作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「參考電極偏移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reference-electrode bias shifts every measured potential. In this model, measured is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.73 V. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Known fixed additive bias. Use independent reference and calibration as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reference-electrode offset” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V；y=measured-offset=0.65 V。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V; y=measured-offset=0.65 V.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「參考電極偏移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reference-electrode offset”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-33-k1","title":"參考電極偏移","titleEn":"Reference-electrode offset","text":"參考電極自身偏差會平移所有量測電位。本模型把 measured 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.73 V。","textEn":"Reference-electrode bias shifts every measured potential. In this model, measured is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「參考電極偏移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reference-electrode offset\" is correct?","options":["參考電極自身偏差會平移所有量測電位。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流"],"optionsEn":["Reference-electrode bias shifts every measured potential.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"參考電極自身偏差會平移所有量測電位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reference-electrode bias shifts every measured potential. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b364-v16-34","title":"參考電極偏移：定量估算","titleEn":"Reference-electrode offset: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「參考電極偏移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reference-electrode offset” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V；y=measured-offset=0.65 V。只把 measured 增加百分之十，y=0.73 V。模型邊界：已知固定加性偏差；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V; y=measured-offset=0.65 V. Increasing only measured with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.73 V. Boundary: Known fixed additive bias; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以獨立參考與校正區分模型與觀察，先用低壓參考源與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use independent reference and calibration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V；y=measured-offset=0.65 V。只把 measured 增加百分之十，y=0.73 V。模型邊界：已知固定加性偏差；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V; y=measured-offset=0.65 V. Increasing only measured with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.73 V. Boundary: Known fixed additive bias; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「參考電極偏移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reference-electrode offset\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：一路中斷會重分配全回路電流","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V；y=measured-offset=0.65 V。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用絕對電流積分會混淆陽極與陰極時段"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Opening one path redistributes total return current.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V; y=measured-offset=0.65 V.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Integrating absolute current confuses anodic and cathodic periods."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V；y=measured-offset=0.65 V。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: measured=0.8 V, offset=0.15 V; y=measured-offset=0.65 V. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b364-v16-35","title":"參考電極偏移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reference-electrode offset: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「參考電極偏移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reference-electrode offset” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以獨立參考與校正區分模型與觀察，先用低壓參考源與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「參考電極偏移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use independent reference and calibration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage reference source and differential meter, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Reference-electrode offset. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「參考電極偏移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出已知固定加性偏差如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差造成偏離的合成觀察，以獨立參考與校正說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Reference-electrode offset, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Known fixed additive bias. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. Explain which evidence in independent reference and calibration distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以獨立參考與校正區分模型與觀察，先用低壓參考源與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「參考電極偏移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use independent reference and calibration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-voltage reference source and differential meter, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Reference-electrode offset. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「參考電極偏移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出已知固定加性偏差如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差造成偏離的合成觀察，以獨立參考與校正說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Reference-electrode offset, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Known fixed additive bias. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. Explain which evidence in independent reference and calibration distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「參考電極偏移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reference-electrode offset\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接觸探針電阻會偽造劣化趨勢","本單元以獨立參考與校正區分模型與觀察，先用低壓參考源與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Probe contact resistance can mimic degradation.","Use independent reference and calibration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以獨立參考與校正區分模型與觀察，先用低壓參考源與差動電表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use independent reference and calibration to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b364-v16-36","title":"參考電極偏移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reference-electrode offset: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「參考電極偏移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reference-electrode offset” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差。這個失效與「參考電極偏移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查獨立參考與校正，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. This failure and a measurement bias in Reference-electrode offset can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check independent reference and calibration rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用獨立參考與校正作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差。這個失效與「參考電極偏移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查獨立參考與校正，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. This failure and a measurement bias in Reference-electrode offset can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check independent reference and calibration rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「參考電極偏移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reference-electrode offset\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流"],"optionsEn":["Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用同一偏移參考重測不會消除偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeating with the same shifted reference does not remove bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b364-v16-37","title":"時間取樣電荷：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sampled charge estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「時間取樣電荷」如何影響鐵路回流與雜散電流控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sampled charge estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rail-return and stray-current control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"梯形積分假定兩樣本間電流線性變化。本模型把 I1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 12.3 C。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。兩樣本線性插值。使用更密集取樣電流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「時間取樣電荷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Trapezoidal integration assumes linear current variation between samples. In this model, I1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 12.3 C. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Linear interpolation between two samples. Use more densely sampled current as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sampled charge estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s；y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s; y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「時間取樣電荷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sampled charge estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-37-k1","title":"時間取樣電荷","titleEn":"Sampled charge estimate","text":"梯形積分假定兩樣本間電流線性變化。本模型把 I1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 12.3 C。","textEn":"Trapezoidal integration assumes linear current variation between samples. In this model, I1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間取樣電荷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sampled charge estimate\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流","梯形積分假定兩樣本間電流線性變化。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals.","Trapezoidal integration assumes linear current variation between samples.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop."],"answer":1,"explanation":"梯形積分假定兩樣本間電流線性變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Trapezoidal integration assumes linear current variation between samples. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b364-v16-38","title":"時間取樣電荷：定量估算","titleEn":"Sampled charge estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「時間取樣電荷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sampled charge estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s；y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C。只把 I1 增加百分之十，y=12.3 C。模型邊界：兩樣本線性插值；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s; y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C. Increasing only I1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=12.3 C. Boundary: Linear interpolation between two samples; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以更密集取樣電流區分模型與觀察，先用合成電流與降採樣比較建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use more densely sampled current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s；y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C。只把 I1 增加百分之十，y=12.3 C。模型邊界：兩樣本線性插值；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s; y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C. Increasing only I1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=12.3 C. Boundary: Linear interpolation between two samples; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時間取樣電荷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sampled charge estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：軌電位不均時不可用單點代表整段","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：電流效率與局部反應使真實損失不同","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s；y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Nonuniform potential cannot be represented by one point.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Current efficiency and local reactions change real material loss.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s; y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s；y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I1=0.1 A, I2=0.3 A, dt=60 s; y=(I1+I2)/2*dt=12 C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b364-v16-39","title":"時間取樣電荷：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sampled charge estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「時間取樣電荷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sampled charge estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以更密集取樣電流區分模型與觀察，先用合成電流與降採樣比較建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「時間取樣電荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use more densely sampled current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic current and downsampling comparison, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sampled charge estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「時間取樣電荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩樣本線性插值如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流造成偏離的合成觀察，以更密集取樣電流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sampled charge estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear interpolation between two samples. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. Explain which evidence in more densely sampled current distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以更密集取樣電流區分模型與觀察，先用合成電流與降採樣比較建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「時間取樣電荷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use more densely sampled current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic current and downsampling comparison, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sampled charge estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「時間取樣電荷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩樣本線性插值如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流造成偏離的合成觀察，以更密集取樣電流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sampled charge estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear interpolation between two samples. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. Explain which evidence in more densely sampled current distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時間取樣電荷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sampled charge estimate\"?","options":["本單元以更密集取樣電流區分模型與觀察，先用合成電流與降採樣比較建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：漏流估計漏項會高估收集效果"],"optionsEn":["Use more densely sampled current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitted leakage paths overstate collection effectiveness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以更密集取樣電流區分模型與觀察，先用合成電流與降採樣比較建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use more densely sampled current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b364-v16-40","title":"時間取樣電荷：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sampled charge estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b364-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「時間取樣電荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sampled charge estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流。這個失效與「時間取樣電荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查更密集取樣電流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. This failure and a measurement bias in Sampled charge estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check more densely sampled current rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用更密集取樣電流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b364-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流。這個失效與「時間取樣電荷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查更密集取樣電流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. This failure and a measurement bias in Sampled charge estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check more densely sampled current rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b364-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時間取樣電荷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sampled charge estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接續線劣化會增加局部壓降"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A degraded bond increases local voltage drop."],"answer":1,"explanation":"稀疏取樣會漏掉短時高電流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sparse sampling misses brief high-current intervals. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b364-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b364-en.svg"}};
